// Program metadata for bluetooth (ADR 0080).
//
// system=true → installed by the profile runner inside arch-chroot as root via
// pacman. install.sh installs bluez + bluez-utils and enables bluetooth.service
// so the Bluetooth daemon comes up on first boot, independent of desktop
// environment selection. Toggle-derived: injected into system_programs from
// options.bluetooth.enabled (default on), so the Bluetooth category is its sole
// home — it never appears in the Packages system-programs picker.

{
  "name": "bluetooth",
  "system": true,
  "description": "Bluetooth daemon (bluez) — installed and enabled at boot."
}
